    "c_content_panel_9rjkLi": {
      "type": "c-content-panel",
      "blocks": {
        "subheading_bxKrEt": {
          "type": "subheading",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Giving Down New Life and a Future: NANGA's Original Upcycling Project"
          }
        },
        "text_jbBt3m": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Down, the feathers of waterfowl, is an excellent material that can last over 100 years with proper care, though this fact is not widely known. As a leading down products company, NANGA started an upcycling service for down comforters, driven by the belief that down should not be treated as a simple consumable, but should be cared for and used for many years. This project, named \"Re:ACT,\" draws on shitatenaoshi, Japan's traditional culture of remaking futons for reuse, and launched in earnest in 2022. We collect worn down comforters from customers, wash the down, and remake it into new NANGA comforters, sleeping bags, or down jackets, then return the finished product to the customer. <strong>(Service available only within Japan)</strong></p><p></p>"
          }
        },
        "text_3CwgH3": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>We offer a bedding series called \"GOOD SLEEPING,\" but we do not want existing futons to be thrown away simply because customers are buying new ones. According to one statistic, the average person in Japan owns the equivalent of 1.8 futons. Considering the environment, we believe existing futons should be actively reused. That is why NANGA offers \"Re:ACT\" as a new option, and we want to grow it into a service that benefits and delights even more users. By reusing down as a resource, we hope to connect it to a future where it can accompany people through outdoor adventures and everyday life, and even serve as an emergency disaster supply when needed. We believe this initiative is meaningful for both the brand and society, and that it can help change attitudes toward reuse.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "subheading_bxKrEt",
        "text_jbBt3m",
        "text_3CwgH3"
      ],
